  "unit": "One catalog provider declared as a direct dependency (including dev, test, optional and workspace declarations) in one dependency-declaring file, in that file's ecosystem. Files Refit does not parse (*.gemspec, setup.py, packages.config) count too.",
  "rules": [
    "A provider package is its official SDK, other packages the provider publishes for its API (Stripe Terminal, Twilio.AspNet helpers), or a general-purpose community client of that API (ruby-openai, gemini-ai, Google_GenerativeAI, async-openai, async-stripe, resend-rs, resendlabs/resend-go).",
    "Framework and gateway adapters that wrap an SDK are not provider packages: Laravel Cashier, Payum and Omnipay gateways, Spring AI starters, DSPy adapters, LangChain integrations.",
    "Azure OpenAI clients (Azure.AI.OpenAI) are not the OpenAI API.",
    "Central version lists (Directory.Packages.props PackageVersion) and Gemfile `gemspec` lines declare nothing by themselves; the file with the PackageReference or add_dependency does.",
    "A repository that is the SDK itself (a fork of sendgrid-python) does not depend on it."
  ],
